Z||000002||Raydar||10-18-2001||10:26 PM||||Just take the circuit board off your old tach and attach it to the new one. Works just fine. The needle sweep is the same, only the scale on the GT tach is calibrated to 7000 RPM. I did the same thing when I put a backlit 86 SE tach in my 88 coupe. <P>Ummm... What are you gonna do for an oil pressure gauge?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
